Test DNS rebinding protection for localhost servers.

[1mScope:[0m This test applies to localhost MCP servers running without HTTPS and without
authentication. These servers are vulnerable to DNS rebinding attacks where a malicious
website tricks a user's browser into making requests to the local server.

[1mAttack scenario:[0m
1. User visits malicious website (e.g., evil.com)
2. evil.com's DNS is configured to resolve to 127.0.0.1
3. Browser makes request to evil.com which actually goes to localhost
4. Without Host/Origin header validation, the local MCP server processes the request

[1mRequirements:[0m
- Server [1mMUST[0m validate the Host or Origin header on incoming requests
- Server [1mMUST[0m reject requests with non-localhost Host/Origin headers (HTTP 4xx)
- Server [1mMUST[0m accept requests with valid localhost Host/Origin headers

[1mValid localhost values:[0m [2mlocalhost[0m, [2m127.0.0.1[0m, [2m[::1][0m (with optional port)

[1mNote:[0m This test requires a localhost server URL. Non-localhost URLs will fail.

